== Match report ==

=== Sanrobonia 4–0 Ayorin ===
[[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] delivered a devastating second-half performance to demolish [[Ayorin national football team|Ayorin]] in [[Castejón]]. The match was goalless at half-time, but Sanrobonia scored four times after the break — in the 51st, 69th, 74th, and 85th minutes — to secure a place in the semi-finals. Ayorin, who had knocked out group winners Tondano in the round of 16, were unable to respond to Sanrobonia's second-half onslaught.

=== Varkana 1–2 Orma ===
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] continued their remarkable run of comebacks at the [[2026 AFA World Cup]], overcoming an early deficit to knock out [[Varkana national football team|Varkana]] in [[Concepción]]. [[Hugo Loria]] had given Varkana the lead in the 2nd minute, but [[Mikael Dirra]] equalised in the 58th minute and [[Yohannes Goba]] struck in the 84th minute to seal the win. Orma had previously come from behind to beat the United Midlands in the round of 16, and their tally of tournament comeback victories now stands at two.

== Summary ==

The opening day of the quarter-finals produced 7 goals across 2 matches. [[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] and [[Orma national football team|Orma]] advanced to the semi-finals. Sanrobonia's 4–0 demolition of Ayorin was the most emphatic result of the knockout stage so far, while Orma's comeback victory over Varkana continued their reputation as the tournament's comeback specialists.

